    "abstract": "This report presents a formal architectural blueprint for a data management\n      framework within TiddlyWiki, analogous to an Object-Relational Mapper (ORM),\n      designed to facilitate large-scale, LLM-driven code refactoring projects. The frame-\n      work introduces a hybrid “Schema-on-Validate” layer that reconciles traditional\n      “schema-on-write” paradigms with TiddlyWiki’s native “schema-on-read” architec-\n      ture. By establishing formal Entity definitions using the Zod validation library,\n      the framework provides explicit, machine-readable schemas that serve as a single\n      source of truth for data validation, static type generation, and LLM instruction.\n      The report details the complete methodology from schema discovery and definition\n      syntax to implementation of ORM functions and advanced templated transclusion\n      patterns, providing a comprehensive roadmap for refactoring complex TiddlyWiki\n      applications.",
